  "text": ".localScale(factor) To determine the maximum number of acute angles that can be formed by the intersection of two line segments connecting two pairs of vertices in a regular hexagon, we need to analyze the geometry of the hexagon.\n\n1. **Understanding the Hexagon**:\n   A regular hexagon has six vertices and can be divided into six equilateral triangles by drawing lines from the center to each vertex.\n\n2. **Line Segments Connecting Pairs of Vertices**:\n   Consider two pairs of vertices in a regular hexagon. The first pair can be chosen in any two vertices, and the second pair can be chosen from the remaining four vertices (since we don't want to repeat the connections).\n\n3. **Intersection of Line Segments**:\n   The line segments connecting the first pair of vertices will intersect the line segments connecting the second pair of vertices. Each pair of vertex and midpoint line segments will intersect at the midpoint of the side opposite to the respective pair of vertices.\n\n4. **Angles at the Intersection**:\n   The angles formed by the intersection of these line segments will depend on the positions of the vertices. The key is to check if any of these angles are acute.\n\n5. **Analyzing the Angles**:\n   - In a regular hexagon, the internal angles at each vertex are 120 degrees.\n   - The line segments connecting the midpoints of the sides to the opposite vertices will intersect at right angles (90 degrees) because the hexagon is regular and the vertices are symmetrically placed.\n   - However, the angles between these line segments and the sides of the hexagon can be acute.\n\n6. **Counting the Acute Angles**:\n   - We can form two acute angles by drawing line segments from a vertex to the midpoint of the side opposite to that vertex, and another pair of such line segments from two different vertices to the midpoints of their opposite sides.\n   - These two pairs of line segments will intersect at the midpoints of the sides opposite to the respective pairs of vertices, forming two acute angles.\n\nTherefore, the maximum number of acute angles that can be formed by the intersection of two line segments connecting two pairs of vertices in a regular hexagon is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
